    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106066" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφλό-της</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ητος</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>blindness,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Democr.
					175
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				353c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				15.142
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>closedness</i> of the <i>foramen caecum</i> (cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφλός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.2
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>UP</u>
				9.10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph. of
			syllables ending in a consonant, <i>closedness,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.738c
			</span></i>.</div>
